01:12:46,666 --> 01:12:52,666
The Big Short is a 2015 American biographical comedy drama film directed by
Adam McKay from a screenplay by McKay and Charles Randolph.

11
01:20:03,333 --> 01:20:09,333
Based on the 2010 book of the same name by Michael Lewis, it depicts how the 2008
financial crisis was triggered by the United States housing bubble.

12
01:27:20,000 --> 01:27:26,000
The film stars Christian Bale, Steve Carell, Ryan Gosling, and Brad Pitt, with John Magaro, Finn
Wittrock, Hamish Linklater, Rafe Spall, Jeremy Strong, and Marisa Tomei in supporting roles.

13
01:34:36,666 --> 01:34:42,666
The Big Short began a limited release in the United States on December 11, 2015,
followed by a wide release on December 23 by Paramount Pictures.

14
01:41:53,333 --> 01:41:59,333
A critical and commercial success, the film grossed $133 million on a $50 million budget and received acclaim for the
performances of the cast (particularly those of Bale and Carell), McKay's direction, editing, and the screenplay.

15
01:49:10,000 --> 01:49:16,000
The film won the Academy Award for Best Adapted Screenplay in addition to nominations for Best
Picture, Best Director, Best Supporting Actor (Bale), and Best Film Editing.

